      },
      "translation": {
        "mode": "prose-faithful",
        "notes": [],
        "english_text": "(David Durai sits smoking a cigarette, drinking with a liquor bottle before him. Beneath the bench where he sits, the boy Sokkalingam is hiding, sweat pouring down his face. David pours himself another glass and drinks... Staggering, he gets up and tries to go to the train compartment’s “toilet”; losing his balance, he opens the train door and is about to put one foot out. At once Sokkalingam cries out, runs up, wraps an arm around his waist and stops him from falling.)"
      }
